WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.220
In this Sprouts Teaching Technique

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.800
we introduce the idea of “Student Leaders”,

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.920
a simple task based method teachers can use to build self-esteem,

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.740
teach responsibility and help students take

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.880
pride in themselves and their classroom.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.280
To create your own student leaders,

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.380
think about activities that your students can help you complete.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.740
Watering plants,

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.420
being in charge of getting you books

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.520
or anything that is easy for them to do

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.560
and makes them feel special.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.120
Next, transform these tasks

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:34.480
into special roles for your students.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.300
Instead of just having your students water your plants,

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.780
give them the title of “Rain-Maker.”

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.140
Instead of getting a book,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.180
name them the “Book-Master”.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.680
Giving these tasks a title will make them excited to help you.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.680
It will also help them pay attention

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.080
and feel good about themselves.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.160
Some tasks can be daily and some every few days.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.000
It helps to create a “Student Leader”

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.160
calendar for all your students to see

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.380
and make sure that you rotate through the tasks

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.680
and that everyone gets a turn at every task.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.640
Please use the comments below

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.060
to let us know what you think!

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.260
If you are a student,

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.260
tell us if you’ve ever been a student leader.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.520
If you are a teacher,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.440
share your tips on how to use this in your classroom.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.380
We’re releasing updates regularly,

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.840
